1	<!DOCTYPE html>
2	<html lang="en">
3	<head>
4	<meta charset="UTF-8">
5	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
6	<title>LeanInference</title>
7	<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
8	<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
9	<style>
10	  :root {
11	    --bg: #0A0E14;
12	    --panel: #111823;
13	    --line: #1F2A38;
14	    --text: #E8EDF3;
15	    --muted: #8A97A8;
16	    --dim: #5B6878;
17	    --mint: #3EE6A8;
18	    --mint-soft: rgba(62, 230, 168, 0.12);
19	    --coral: #FF7A6B;
20	    --coral-soft: rgba(255, 122, 107, 0.12);
21	    --head: 'Space Grotesk', 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
22	    --body: 'Inter', 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
23	  }
24	  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
25	  html, body { height: 100%; background: #05070A; overflow: hidden; }
26	  body { font-family: var(--body); color: var(--text); -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; }
27	
28	  /* Fixed 1600x900 stage, scaled to fit the window */
29	  .stage {
30	    position: absolute; left: 50%; top: 50%;
31	    width: 1600px; height: 900px;
32	    transform-origin: center center;
33	    background: var(--bg);
34	    overflow: hidden;
35	  }
36	  .slide {
37	    position: absolute; inset: 0;
38	    padding: 96px 120px 110px;
39	    display: flex; flex-direction: column;
40	    opacity: 0; visibility: hidden;
41	    transition: opacity .45s ease;
42	  }
43	  .slide.active { opacity: 1; visibility: visible; }
44	  .slide::before { /* soft glow */
45	    content: ''; position: absolute; width: 900px; height: 900px; border-radius: 50%;
46	    background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(62,230,168,0.07), transparent 65%);
47	    right: -300px; top: -360px; pointer-events: none;
48	  }
49	
50	  .brand {
51	    position: absolute; left: 120px; bottom: 48px;
52	    font: 600 18px var(--head); color: var(--dim); letter-spacing: .02em;
53	  }
54	  .brand b { color: var(--mint); font-weight: 600; }
55	
56	  .kicker {
57	    font: 600 18px var(--head); letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase;
58	    color: var(--mint); margin-bottom: 22px;
59	  }
60	  h1 { font: 700 104px/1.02 var(--head); letter-spacing: -.035em; }
61	  h2 { font: 700 60px/1.08 var(--head); letter-spacing: -.025em; max-width: 1300px; }
62	  h3 { font: 600 28px/1.2 var(--head); letter-spacing: -.01em; }
63	  p.lead { font-size: 28px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--muted); max-width: 1150px; margin-top: 28px; }
64	  .mint { color: var(--mint); }
65	  .coral { color: var(--coral); }
66	  .muted { color: var(--muted); }
67	
68	  /* Animations on enter */
69	  .slide.active .rise { animation: rise .7s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1) both; }
70	  .slide.active .rise.d1 { animation-delay: .08s; }
71	  .slide.active .rise.d2 { animation-delay: .16s; }
72	  .slide.active .rise.d3 { animation-delay: .24s; }
73	  .slide.active .rise.d4 { animation-delay: .32s; }
74	  .slide.active .rise.d5 { animation-delay: .40s; }
75	  @keyframes rise { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(24px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: none; } }
76	
77	  /* Title slide */
78	  .title-slide { justify-content: center; }
79	  .title-slide h1 .mint { display: block; }
80	  .title-slide .sub { font-size: 32px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 40px; max-width: 1000px; line-height: 1.4; }
81	  .logo-mark { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 56px; font: 600 30px var(--head); }
82	  .logo-mark i { width: 18px; height: 18px; border-radius: 5px; background: var(--mint); box-shadow: 0 0 30px var(--mint); }
83	
84	  /* Cards */
85	  .grid { display: grid; gap: 28px; margin-top: 56px; }
86	  .g3 { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
87	  .g4 { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
88	  .card {
89	    background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 22px;
90	    padding: 40px 38px;
91	  }
92	  .card p { font-size: 22px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 14px; }
93	  .card .num { font: 700 20px var(--head); color: var(--mint); margin-bottom: 26px; letter-spacing: .1em; }
94	  .card.hl { border-color: rgba(62,230,168,.45); background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(62,230,168,.08), var(--panel) 60%); }
95	
96	  /* Problem slide */
97	  .bill { display: flex; align-items: flex-end; gap: 22px; height: 300px; margin-top: 60px; }
98	  .bill .bar { width: 88px; border-radius: 12px 12px 4px 4px; background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--coral), rgba(255,122,107,.25)); }
99	  .bill-wrap { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; align-items: end; flex: 1; }
100	  .bill-labels { display: flex; gap: 22px; margin-top: 14px; }
101	  .bill-labels span { width: 88px; text-align: center; font-size: 18px; color: var(--dim); }
102	  .pains { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 34px; padding-bottom: 20px; }
103	  .pain { display: flex; gap: 22px; align-items: flex-start; }
104	  .pain .dot { flex: none; width: 12px; height: 12px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--coral); margin-top: 13px; }
105	  .pain div { font-size: 26px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--muted); }
106	  .pain b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
107	
108	  /* Process flow */
109	  .flow { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 64px 1fr 64px 1fr; align-items: stretch; margin-top: 64px; }
110	  .arrow { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; color: var(--dim); font-size: 40px; }
111	
112	  /* Options ladder */
113	  .ladder { margin-top: 56px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; }
114	  .rung { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 420px 1fr 260px; align-items: center; gap: 36px;
115	    background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 18px; padding: 26px 36px; }
116	  .rung h3 { font-size: 26px; }
117	  .rung p { font-size: 21px; color: var(--muted); }
118	  .rung .tag { justify-self: end; font: 600 17px var(--head); letter-spacing: .06em; padding: 9px 18px; border-radius: 99px;
119	    background: var(--mint-soft); color: var(--mint); }
120	  .rung.top .tag { background: var(--coral-soft); color: var(--coral); }
121	
122	  /* Case slides */
123	  .case { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 640px; gap: 80px; flex: 1; margin-top: 40px; }
124	  .case .left p.lead { font-size: 25px; margin-top: 22px; }
125	  .facts { margin-top: 40px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 22px; }
126	  .fact { display: flex; gap: 20px; align-items: baseline; font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--muted); }
127	  .fact b { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
128	  .fact .check { flex: none; color: var(--mint); font-weight: 700; }
129	  .money { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 26px; padding: 46px 48px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
130	  .money .label { font: 600 16px var(--head); letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--dim); }
131	  .money .row { margin-top: 26px; }
132	  .money .row .top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; font-size: 21px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 12px; }
133	  .money .row .top b { font: 700 34px var(--head); color: var(--text); }
134	  .track { height: 22px; border-radius: 99px; background: #0C121B; overflow: hidden; }
135	  .fill { height: 100%; border-radius: 99px; width: 0; transition: width 1.1s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.2,1) .25s; }
136	  .fill.old { background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(255,122,107,.5), var(--coral)); }
137	  .fill.new { background: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(62,230,168,.5), var(--mint)); min-width: 22px; }
138	  .money .save { margin-top: auto; padding-top: 36px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 20px; }
139	  .money .save .big { font: 700 110px/1 var(--head); color: var(--mint); letter-spacing: -.04em; }
140	  .money .save span { font-size: 22px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.35; }
141	  .pill { display: inline-block; font: 600 16px var(--head); letter-spacing: .1em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 8px 16px;
142	    border-radius: 99px; border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); margin-right: 10px; }
143	
144	  /* Summary */
145	  .sum { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 28px; margin-top: 56px; }
146	  .sum .card { padding: 44px 40px; }
147	  .sum .pct { font: 700 120px/1 var(--head); color: var(--mint); letter-spacing: -.045em; }
148	  .sum .what { font: 600 24px var(--head); margin-top: 18px; }
149	  .sum p { font-size: 21px; }
150	  .honest { margin-top: 36px; display: flex; gap: 22px; align-items: center; font-size: 23px; color: var(--muted);
151	    border: 1px dashed var(--line); border-radius: 18px; padding: 24px 32px; }
152	  .honest b { color: var(--text); }
153	
154	  /* Business */
155	  .tiers { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 28px; margin-top: 56px; }
156	  .tier .step { font: 600 16px var(--head); letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--dim); }
157	  .tier h3 { font-size: 38px; margin-top: 14px; }
158	  .tier ul { list-style: none; margin-top: 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px; }
159	  .tier li { font-size: 21px; color: var(--muted); padding-left: 26px; position: relative; line-height: 1.4; }
160	  .tier li::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 11px; width: 8px; height: 8px; border-radius: 2px; background: var(--mint); }
161	  .who { margin-top: 40px; font-size: 24px; color: var(--muted); }
162	  .who b { color: var(--text); }
163	
164	  /* Future */
165	  .future { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 120px 1fr; align-items: stretch; margin-top: 64px; }
166	  .future .card { min-height: 270px; }
167	  .future .card h3 { font-size: 40px; margin-top: 12px; }
168	  .future .when { font: 600 16px var(--head); letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--dim); }
169	  .future .card.hl .when { color: var(--mint); }
170	  .future .big-arrow { align-self: center; text-align: center; font-size: 56px; color: var(--mint); }
171	  .closing { margin-top: 48px; font: 500 30px var(--head); color: var(--text); }
172	  .closing span { color: var(--mint); }
173	
174	  /* Nav */
175	  .progress { position: fixed; left: 0; top: 0; height: 3px; background: var(--mint); transition: width .35s; z-index: 10; }
176	  .counter { position: fixed; right: 28px; bottom: 22px; font: 500 14px var(--body); color: #3C4757; z-index: 10; user-select: none; }
177	
178	  /* Overview (?all) and print: every slide stacked, no animation */
179	  body.all { overflow: auto; background: var(--bg); }
180	  body.all .stage { position: static; transform: none !important; height: auto; }
181	  body.all .slide, body.all .slide * { animation: none !important; }
182	  body.all .slide { position: relative; height: 900px; opacity: 1; visibility: visible; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
183	  body.all .fill { transition: none; }
184	  body.all .progress, body.all .counter { display: none; }
185	  @page { size: 1600px 900px; margin: 0; }
186	  @media print {
187	    body { overflow: visible; background: var(--bg); -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact; }
188	    .stage { position: static; transform: none !important; height: auto; }
189	    .slide, .slide * { animation: none !important; transition: none !important; }
190	    .slide { position: relative; height: 900px; opacity: 1; visibility: visible; break-after: page; }
191	    .progress, .counter { display: none; }
192	  }
193	</style>
194	</head>
195	<body>
196	<div class="progress" id="progress"></div>
197	<div class="stage" id="stage">
198	
199	  <!-- 1. Title -->
200	  <section class="slide title-slide active">
201	    <div class="logo-mark rise"><i></i>LeanInference</div>
202	    <h1 class="rise d1">Your AI bill is<span class="mint">bigger than it needs to be.</span></h1>
203	    <p class="sub rise d2">Most startups use a top-tier model for everything. For a lot of tasks, a small model trained on your own data does the same job for much less. We test that properly before you change anything.</p>
204	  </section>
205	
206	  <!-- 2. Problem -->
207	  <section class="slide">
208	    <div class="kicker rise">The problem</div>
209	    <h2 class="rise d1">Most AI startups send <span class="coral">every</span> request to the biggest model.</h2>
210	    <div class="bill-wrap">
211	      <div class="rise d2">
212	        <div class="bill">
213	          <div class="bar" style="height:16%"></div>
214	          <div class="bar" style="height:28%"></div>
215	          <div class="bar" style="height:45%"></div>
216	          <div class="bar" style="height:70%"></div>
217	          <div class="bar" style="height:100%"></div>
218	        </div>
219	        <div class="bill-labels"><span>M1</span><span>M2</span><span>M3</span><span>M4</span><span>M5</span></div>
220	        <p class="muted" style="font-size:20px;margin-top:18px">What a typical AI bill does as a product grows.</p>
221	      </div>
222	      <div class="pains">
223	        <div class="pain rise d2"><i class="dot"></i><div><b>It's overkill.</b> Tagging a ticket or filling in a form is a small job. It doesn't need the most expensive model on the market.</div></div>
224	        <div class="pain rise d3"><i class="dot"></i><div><b>The bill grows with every user.</b> Great for usage, not so great for margins.</div></div>
225	        <div class="pain rise d4"><i class="dot"></i><div><b>Customer data ends up on someone else's servers.</b> For insurance or health companies, that's a real problem.</div></div>
226	      </div>
227	    </div>
228	    <div class="brand"><b>■</b> LeanInference</div>
229	  </section>
230	
231	  <!-- 3. How it works -->
232	  <section class="slide">
233	    <div class="kicker rise">How we work</div>
234	    <h2 class="rise d1">We test <span class="mint">first</span>. You only switch if the numbers hold up.</h2>
235	    <div class="flow">
236	      <div class="card rise d2"><div class="num">01</div><h3>Measure</h3><p>We take real requests from your product and write down what the right answer is for each one.</p></div>
237	      <div class="arrow rise d2">→</div>
238	      <div class="card rise d3"><div class="num">02</div><h3>Compare</h3><p>Your current model and the cheaper options all run on that same test. We compare accuracy, speed and cost.</p></div>
239	      <div class="arrow rise d3">→</div>
240	      <div class="card hl rise d4"><div class="num">03</div><h3>Ship</h3><p>If something cheaper is just as good, we put it into production. If nothing is, we tell you that too.</p></div>
241	    </div>
242	    <div class="brand"><b>■</b> LeanInference</div>
243	  </section>
244	
245	  <!-- 4. Options -->
246	  <section class="slide">
247	    <div class="kicker rise">What we try</div>
248	    <h2 class="rise d1">There's usually a smaller model that can do the job.</h2>
249	    <div class="ladder">
250	      <div class="rung top rise d2"><h3>Frontier model</h3><p>What most startups use today, for pretty much everything.</p><span class="tag">$$$$ · THIRD PARTY</span></div>
251	      <div class="rung rise d3"><h3>Cheaper hosted model</h3><p>A smaller model from the same kind of provider, with a better prompt.</p><span class="tag">$$ · THIRD PARTY</span></div>
252	      <div class="rung rise d4"><h3>Small fine-tuned model</h3><p>An open-source model we train on your task. You own it, and it runs on your servers.</p><span class="tag">$ · YOUR CLOUD</span></div>
253	      <div class="rung rise d5"><h3>Classic ML</h3><p>For simple labelling jobs, a plain classifier is often enough. No LLM needed.</p><span class="tag">¢ · ANYWHERE</span></div>
254	    </div>
255	    <div class="brand"><b>■</b> LeanInference</div>
256	  </section>
257	
258	  <!-- 5. Case 1 -->
259	  <section class="slide">
260	    <div class="kicker rise">Case study 1 · Logistics app</div>
261	    <div class="case">
262	      <div class="left">
263	        <h2 class="rise d1" style="font-size:54px">Routely: turning chat into actions</h2>
264	        <p class="lead rise d2">An in-app assistant turns "move my Tuesday pickup to Thursday 3pm" into one of 40 API actions. <b style="color:var(--text)">2M requests a month.</b></p>
265	        <div class="facts">
266	          <div class="fact rise d3"><span class="check">✓</span><div>After fine-tuning, a small 2B model <b>picks the right action 97.9%</b> of the time.</div></div>
267	          <div class="fact rise d3"><span class="check">✓</span><div>The old setup sent <b>5,300 tokens of tool descriptions</b> with every request. The trained model doesn't need them.</div></div>
268	          <div class="fact rise d4"><span class="check">✓</span><div>It mixes up similar actions, like cancel order vs. cancel pickup, <b>less often than the cheaper hosted model</b>.</div></div>
269	          <div class="fact rise d4"><span class="check">✓</span><div>It runs on Routely's own servers.</div></div>
270	        </div>
271	      </div>
272	      <div class="money rise d2">
273	        <div class="label">Monthly cost</div>
274	        <div class="row"><div class="top">Frontier model today <b>$116,080</b></div><div class="track"><div class="fill old" data-w="100"></div></div></div>
275	        <div class="row"><div class="top">Cheaper hosted model <b>$3,005</b></div><div class="track"><div class="fill new" data-w="2.6"></div></div></div>
276	        <div class="row"><div class="top">Our fine-tuned 2B model <b class="mint">$1,292</b></div><div class="track"><div class="fill new" data-w="1.1"></div></div></div>
277	        <div class="save"><div class="big">−99%</div><span>about $1.4M<br>a year saved</span></div>
278	      </div>
279	    </div>
280	    <div class="brand"><b>■</b> LeanInference</div>
281	  </section>
282	
283	  <!-- 6. Case 2 -->
284	  <section class="slide">
285	    <div class="kicker rise">Case study 2 · Insurtech</div>
286	    <div class="case">
287	      <div class="left">
288	        <h2 class="rise d1" style="font-size:54px">ClaimPilot: claim documents to data</h2>
289	        <p class="lead rise d2">Invoices, medical bills and repair quotes get turned into clean data for their claims system. <b style="color:var(--text)">500K documents a month.</b></p>
290	        <div class="facts">
291	          <div class="fact rise d3"><span class="check">✓</span><div>After fine-tuning, a tiny 0.8B model <b>did better than the frontier model</b> in our tests.</div></div>
292	          <div class="fact rise d3"><span class="check">✓</span><div>Documents with every field right: <b>93.8% vs 69.2%</b>.</div></div>
293	          <div class="fact rise d4"><span class="check">✓</span><div>Payout amounts right: <b>99.5% vs 95.8%</b>. If a field was missing, it left it empty instead of guessing.</div></div>
294	          <div class="fact rise d4"><span class="check">✓</span><div>The documents <b>never leave ClaimPilot's servers</b>, which takes care of their compliance worry.</div></div>
295	        </div>
296	      </div>
297	      <div class="money rise d2">
298	        <div class="label">Monthly cost</div>
299	        <div class="row"><div class="top">Frontier model today <b>$5,132</b></div><div class="track"><div class="fill old" data-w="100"></div></div></div>
300	        <div class="row"><div class="top">Our fine-tuned 0.8B model <b class="mint">$861</b></div><div class="track"><div class="fill new" data-w="16.8"></div></div></div>
301	        <div class="row" style="margin-top:34px"><span class="pill">More accurate</span><span class="pill">Private</span></div>
302	        <div class="save"><div class="big">−83%</div><span>and fewer<br>mistakes</span></div>
303	      </div>
304	    </div>
305	    <div class="brand"><b>■</b> LeanInference</div>
306	  </section>
307	
308	  <!-- 7. Case 3 -->
309	  <section class="slide">
310	    <div class="kicker rise">Case study 3 · Customer support</div>
311	    <div class="case">
312	      <div class="left">
313	        <h2 class="rise d1" style="font-size:54px">Helpdeskly: ticket triage</h2>
314	        <p class="lead rise d2">Every ticket gets tagged with a topic, how urgent it is, and the customer's mood, then goes to the right team. <b style="color:var(--text)">1M tickets a month.</b></p>
315	        <div class="facts">
316	          <div class="fact rise d3"><span class="check">✓</span><div>They were paying for a frontier model <b>to output three words</b>.</div></div>
317	          <div class="fact rise d3"><span class="check">✓</span><div>Our fine-tuned 0.8B model got <b>topic and mood right on all 700</b> test tickets.</div></div>
318	          <div class="fact rise d4"><span class="check">✓</span><div>It <b>flags urgent tickets</b> about as well as the frontier model.</div></div>
319	          <div class="fact rise d4"><span class="check">✓</span><div>Want it even cheaper? A simple classifier, no LLM at all, gets 97% on topic for <b>$130 a month</b>.</div></div>
320	        </div>
321	      </div>
322	      <div class="money rise d2">
323	        <div class="label">Monthly cost</div>
324	        <div class="row"><div class="top">Frontier model today <b>$1,120</b></div><div class="track"><div class="fill old" data-w="100"></div></div></div>
325	        <div class="row"><div class="top">Our fine-tuned 0.8B model <b class="mint">$431</b></div><div class="track"><div class="fill new" data-w="38.5"></div></div></div>
326	        <div class="row"><div class="top">Simple classifier <b class="mint">$130</b></div><div class="track"><div class="fill new" data-w="11.6"></div></div></div>
327	        <div class="save"><div class="big">−62%</div><span>or −88% with the<br>simple classifier</span></div>
328	      </div>
329	    </div>
330	    <div class="brand"><b>■</b> LeanInference</div>
331	  </section>
332	
333	  <!-- 8. Summary -->
334	  <section class="slide">
335	    <div class="kicker rise">So far</div>
336	    <h2 class="rise d1">Three very different jobs, same outcome.</h2>
337	    <div class="sum">
338	      <div class="card rise d2"><div class="pct">−99%</div><div class="what">Routely · actions</div><p>$116K → $1.3K a month</p></div>
339	      <div class="card rise d3"><div class="pct">−83%</div><div class="what">ClaimPilot · documents</div><p>$5.1K → $0.9K a month</p></div>
340	      <div class="card rise d4"><div class="pct">−62%</div><div class="what">Helpdeskly · triage</div><p>$1.1K → $0.4K a month</p></div>
341	    </div>
342	    <div class="honest rise d5"><div><b>Not everything worked.</b> We also tried a tiny on-device model in all three cases. It wasn't good enough yet, so we didn't recommend it. We'd rather say that than sell something that doesn't hold up.</div></div>
343	    <div class="brand"><b>■</b> LeanInference</div>
344	  </section>
345	
346	  <!-- 9. Business -->
347	  <section class="slide">
348	    <div class="kicker rise">How we make money</div>
349	    <h2 class="rise d1">The savings pay for us.</h2>
350	    <div class="tiers">
351	      <div class="card tier rise d2"><div class="step">Step 1</div><h3>Audit</h3><ul><li>Fixed price, about 2 weeks</li><li>We build the test from their data</li><li>They see what they'd save</li></ul></div>
352	      <div class="card tier hl rise d3"><div class="step" style="color:var(--mint)">Step 2</div><h3>Build</h3><ul><li>We train or set up the cheaper model</li><li>Deploy it on their servers</li><li>They own the model</li></ul></div>
353	      <div class="card tier rise d4"><div class="step">Step 3</div><h3>Run</h3><ul><li>Monthly fee</li><li>We keep an eye on quality</li><li>Retrain when things change</li></ul></div>
354	    </div>
355	    <p class="who rise d5"><b>Who we're going after:</b> startups with a growing AI bill. Insurance, health and finance first, because they also care where their data goes.</p>
356	    <div class="brand"><b>■</b> LeanInference</div>
357	  </section>
358	
359	  <!-- 10. Future -->
360	  <section class="slide">
361	    <div class="kicker rise">Later on</div>
362	    <h2 class="rise d1">Start as a service, then automate it.</h2>
363	    <div class="future">
364	      <div class="card rise d2"><div class="when">Now</div><h3>Hands-on service</h3><p>Right now we do every project by hand. That's on purpose: it's how we learn what actually works.</p></div>
365	      <div class="big-arrow rise d3">→</div>
366	      <div class="card hl rise d4"><div class="when">Next</div><h3>Mostly automated</h3><p>Later, we want to turn what we've learned into software that does most of this on its own, so we can take on far more clients.</p></div>
367	    </div>
368	    <p class="closing rise d5">For now, the focus is landing our first real clients.</p>
369	    <div class="brand"><b>■</b> LeanInference</div>
370	  </section>
